DETAILED AGENT PROMPT — Fix Empty/White Area After Hiding Select Arrow

Problem Summary
After hiding the dropdown arrow on the product <select>, a blank/white area appears, and the product text does not expand to use the freed space. We need to keep the arrow hidden but allow the product name to occupy the full width.

Goal
Remove the blank area and make the product name text visible across the full width of the Product column, without changing table layout, widths, or any other behavior.

Constraints
- Do NOT change column widths or table structure.
- Do NOT replace the <select> element.
- Do NOT alter calculations, data, or any other UI.

Root Cause (Common)
Most browsers reserve space for the dropdown arrow using internal padding or background. When appearance is removed, the padding or background may still remain, leaving an empty area.

Fix Strategy (Minimal, Safe)
1) Remove arrow styling AND remove extra padding reserved for the arrow.
2) Ensure the select text fills the available width.
3) Keep the select background consistent with inputs.

Implementation Steps
1) Add a CSS class to product selects AFTER selection:
	 - class: .selected (already used to hide arrow)

2) Apply the following CSS for product selects ONLY:
	 - Remove native appearance.
	 - Reset background image.
	 - Reset padding-right to a small value so text expands.
	 - Force text to occupy full width and align left or center as desired.

Exact CSS (Scope to Product Column Only)
- #invTable td:first-child select.selected {
		appearance: none;
		-webkit-appearance: none;
		-moz-appearance: none;
		background-image: none !important;
		background-color: #fff; /* match input bg */
		padding-right: 6px; /* remove reserved arrow space */
		text-indent: 0; /* remove hidden offset */
		overflow: visible; /* allow full text */
	}
- #invTable td:first-child select.selected::-ms-expand { display: none; }

Optional (If still truncated)
- #invTable td:first-child select {
		width: 100%;
		white-space: nowrap; /* or normal if you allow wrap */
		text-overflow: ellipsis; /* if keeping single line */
	}

If you want full text without ellipsis:
- Use white-space: normal and word-break: break-word (only on product column).

JS Hook (If not already present)
On change event for the product <select>:
- if (this.value) this.classList.add('selected');
- else this.classList.remove('selected');

Acceptance Criteria
- No blank/white area after arrow is hidden.
- Product text uses full width of the column.
- Dropdown still opens and works normally.
- No layout changes to other columns.

